      "text": "Hello, welcome to my presentation at the Artificial Intelligence for Information Accessibility Conference. My name is Okambolo. I'm a professor in the measurement, evaluation, and data science program at the University of Alberta, Canada. In this presentation, I will be talking about the evolution of assessment literacy in the era of AI, and why assessment literacy should be considered a pillar of AI literacy in higher education. Over the last few years, many genetic AI tools have become accessible, such as Open Apps, JetGPT, Google's Gemini, and Mata's Lama. These tools are capable of generating text, images, audios, and videos based on some user prompts. The increased availability and accessibility of these tools have influenced many fields",
