      "text": "including higher education. The Digital Council, Education Council conducted a comprehensive survey back in 2024 with around 4,000 responses from undergraduate and graduate students across 16 countries. The results of this survey offer a diverse range of student viewpoints on AI in education. For instance, 86% of the students reported using AI in their daily studies, and approximately 54% of the students use genetic AI tools at least once a week. These findings suggest that students have already incorporated AI into their learning processes. Also, most students just reported using genetic AI for searching for information as if they were searching for information in a search engine such as Google. Students also reported other use cases of AI such as checking grammar, summarizing documents",
